{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011CevjW33LL6QR8GqYQyka9","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I've completed the independent blind analysis. A note on evidence access: the host interface returned \"success\" for my `read_files` calls but did not surface the contents of `harness/planner.py`, its tests, or the other collaborator modules I requested. Per the instruction not to claim to have read files the host has not returned, I based the analysis strictly on the request text and the artifacts the host did provide (the pinned v0.3.0 contract, registry, per-question schemas, `_index.json`, golden cases, input-catalog snapshot, `rules.md`, and `docs/decisions.md`), and I explicitly flagged every planner-implementation claim as **missing evidence** with the observation that would confirm or disprove it.\n\nThe delivered Markdown covers all six required sections, with the load-bearing concern being requirement (5): the current `RepairCapExceeded → Unsupported` path (ADR-014) is exactly the conflation the request wants removed, and a plan could satisfy the other four verbs while leaving it intact. The O-8 `xfail` interaction and the \"derive required inputs vs. usurp the data layer's defaulting\" tension are the other two highest-risk items."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":8800,"cache_read_input_tokens":70655,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":8800},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b2597576-7535-47bb-ba13-f117ef1d4936","uuid":"c92f1346-94dc-4029-b867-df2a6038d011","request_id":"req_011CevjW1DwnHgPUM4KtcWps"}
